1
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,200
Attention.

2
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:53,560
The vehicle-mounted 30mm cannons

3
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,880
and the firing arcs of the anti-aircraft machine guns

4
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,200
must follow combat readiness standards.

5
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,280
What's the use of just looking neat?

6
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,520
What's wrong with looking neat?

7
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,960
Can looking neat win a battle?

8
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,080
Can looking good win a battle?

9
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:05,840
Can looking good win a battle?

10
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:07,880
Put your hand down.

11
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,800
Pay attention.

12
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,040
What's going on here?

13
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,960
Report, Comrade Deputy Brigade Commander.

14
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:19,080
Wind Rider Battalion's special ops platoon is parking.

15
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:20,120
Awaiting orders.

16
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:22,400
Special Ops Platoon Leader Yang Maolin.

17
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:23,440
Acting.

18
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:23,920
Yes, sir.

19
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,680
Acting Platoon Leader Yang Maolin.

20
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,400
How are these vehicles parked?

21
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,400
It's a complete mess.

22
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:33,480
Where is your battalion commander?

23
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:35,120
Report, sir.

24
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,440
Our battalion command post

25
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,040
is 500 meters to my right rear.

26
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,360
Adjust the vehicles.

27
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:42,600
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

28
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:45,040
We parked this way based on the terrain

29
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,200
for tactical deployment.

30
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:48,840
Each vehicle has adjusted its weapon's firing arc,

31
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,840
responsible for guarding different directions.

32
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:52,120
If enemy activity is detected,

33
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,200
we ensure we can attack, defend, and retreat.

34
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,040
Having enemy awareness is right.

35
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:57,680
But...

36
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,360
but you must know the right time and place.

37
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:01,800
Our battalion commander said...

38
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:03,520
Pass my words on to your battalion commander.

39
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:04,720
Yes, sir.

40
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,360
Why all the nonsense?

41
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:10,840
Hurry up and adjust the vehicles.

42
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,160
Don't say I didn't warn you.

43
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:20,160
Just drop it.

44
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,840
Yang Maolin.

45
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,360
Being Acting Platoon Leader is no big deal.

46
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,560
You know better than anyone

47
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,800
whose position this should have been.

48
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:28,720
Right?

49
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:33,200
You can never replace him.

50
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,880
You can't replace his Golden Right Foot.

51
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:44,040
The design of this operation plan was full of flaws,

52
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,680
causing the operation to fall short of expectations.

53
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,880
I bear undeniable responsibility for this.

54
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:50,360
Therefore,

55
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:52,640
I officially request

56
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,240
to receive disciplinary action.

57
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:01,880
Sit.

58
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:09,880
Staff Officer Liang,

59
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,480
All your life,

60
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,080
how many times have you admitted you were wrong?

61
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,360
Why do you ask that?

62
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,440
Just curious.

63
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,040
Childhood doesn't count.

64
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,760
Just since becoming an adult,

65
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,320
how many times have you admitted you were wrong?

66
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,520
I don't think I actually have.

67
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,360
Because I have

68
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:34,960
never made a mistake.

69
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,960
That's exactly the problem.

70
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,000
Because no one can avoid making mistakes forever.

71
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:43,080
No matter how thoroughly you plan,

72
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:46,840
the reality of the situation will always change.

73
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:49,200
That's why they say plans can't keep up with changes.

74
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,120
The problem is, my plan wasn't thorough enough.

75
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,360
First,

76
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:54,600
before we set off,

77
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,240
I did take the weather conditions

78
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,240
into account.

79
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,720
But I failed to consider

80
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:01,640
that the hydrology and geology of the Majia River area

81
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,800
have changed significantly recently.

82
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,240
I used data from earlier this year,

83
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,840
but this data was updated two weeks ago,

84
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,360
and I didn't notice.

85
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,040
Second,

86
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,360
when formulating the plan,

87
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,800
for every company in the Wind Rider Battalion,

88
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,240
I analyzed their daily basic training scores

89
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,600
and compiled the statistics.

90
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,160
But some of those training scores

91
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,240
were based on simulated training.

92
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,840
The discrepancy between simulated and actual combat drills

93
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:25,960
was something I didn't consider enough.

94
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,200
So you're right, Battalion Commander.

95
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,000
I'm not a qualified staff officer.

96
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,200
You're wrong again.

97
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,240
This goes to show exactly

98
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,720
that you are a qualified staff officer.

99
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,000
The purpose of our training,

100
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,640
besides reinforcing our skills,

101
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,920
is to find problems

102
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:46,960
and solve them.

103
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:48,960
Aside from issues with training subjects,

104
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,480
there are also issues with our officers and soldiers.

105
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,880
So in this sense,

106
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,440
you're doing very well right now.

107
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,600
On this point,

108
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,200
I concede to you.

109
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:02,280
Remember our first clash with the 404th Brigade?

110
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,160
Because of my stubbornness,

111
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,120
I fell into Long Yuanshan's trap.

112
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,520
But even after that crushing defeat,

113
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,440
I still felt it wasn't my fault.

114
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,800
I just thought we were only slightly bested

115
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:16,000
on timing,

116
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,000
and I even blamed the failure of the exercise

117
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,040
on the incompetence of others.

118
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,360
If I had been like you back then

119
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,680
and faced my own mistakes head-on,

120
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:26,000
maybe I wouldn't have taken so many detours.

121
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,480
So, Staff Officer Liang,

122
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,480
let's make another pact.

123
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,040
From now on in the Wind Rider Battalion,

124
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,040
we will be each other's mirrors.

125
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:37,000
When one of us falls into the trap of subjective judgment,

126
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,280
we will remind the other,

127
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:41,160
to minimize the probability of errors occurring.

128
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:42,360
How about it?

129
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,800
All right.

130
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,280
You have my word.

131
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,480
Today,

132
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,560
leaders of both battalions are here.

133
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,440
I'm announcing a decision.

134
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:10,040
The field training units will suspend field training for now.

135
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,560
After adapting to the situation,

136
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,400
basic training

137
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:15,880
and consolidation

138
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,000
will be conducted together.

139
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,440
I agree.

140
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,560
What are you looking at me for?

141
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,640
The sun must have risen in the west.

142
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,440
I resolutely obey the leadership's arrangements,

143
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,080
and will never act like a maverick.

144
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,880
Aren't you embarrassed saying that?

145
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,440
I'm stating my position to our leader.

146
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:42,520
What is there to be embarrassed about?

147
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,040
Good.

148
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:45,840
Then tell me,

149
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,040
how will you consolidate?

150
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,760
According to your instructions,

151
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,600
we'll readjust the training plan.

152
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:53,920
Readjust how?

153
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:56,720
You warned me before.

154
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:59,800
Taking too big a step can lead to a fall.

155
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:00,880
Facts have proven that

156
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,840
experience counts.

157
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,760
If the foundation is weak, the whole structure will crumble.

158
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,880
If you have this understanding,

159
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,880
it means your setback wasn't in vain.

160
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,680
But Deputy Brigade Commander,

161
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,800
time is combat effectiveness.

162
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,480
Isn't a week of consolidation a bit long?

163
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,520
One or two days should be enough.

164
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:19,440
And then we can

165
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,080
focus on basic training subjects.

166
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,600
Don't try to sweet-talk me.

167
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,960
A stitch in time saves nine.

168
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,480
First unify your training thoughts,

169
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:31,600
and make detailed operational plans.

170
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:35,320
Isn't that better than riding blind

171
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,320
and acting recklessly?

172
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:37,760
Deputy Brigade Commander,

173
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,240
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo is absolutely right.

174
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,360
If the foundation is weak, the whole structure will crumble.

175
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:42,960
Setbacks shouldn't be in vain.

176
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:43,760
Right.

177
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,080
Bringing your two field training teams out

178
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:47,960
is to let you

179
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:48,920
compete, learn, catch up,

180
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:49,560
help, and surpass each other.

181
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,240
First, both your battalions

182
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,000
must learn from each other

183
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,320
and progress together.

184
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:57,960
Brilliant, Deputy Brigade Commander.

185
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,080
Then how about this?

186
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,040
In half a month,

187
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:01,440
our two battalions

188
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:04,680
will hold a major basic training competition.

189
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,840
What do you say, Battalion Commander Jiang?

190
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:07,680
Fine.

191
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,120
Anytime.

192
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,520
Units holding contests and competitions,

193
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,280
I don't oppose that.

194
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:15,840
However,

195
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,160
let me emphasize one point.

196
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,800
Comprehensive consolidation

197
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:20,720
must be implemented.

198
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:21,920
Yes, sir!

199
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,520
It's a blessing Jiang Shengqiang isn't provoking you.

200
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,680
Why do you have to provoke him?

201
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,560
We came out for field training

202
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,440
to improve our combat effectiveness, right?

203
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:40,520
Since Hurricane Battalion was established,

204
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,520
they've been training behind closed doors every day.

205
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,360
Who knows what unparalleled skills they're practicing?

206
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,160
With such a ready-made opponent,

207
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:48,400
wouldn't it be a waste not to practice on him?

208
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,400
Fine.

209
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,840
You always make so much sense.

210
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,960
Then keep competing and fighting.

211
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,080
That's how the group army arranged it anyway.

212
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,440
It's to let you clash.

213
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:58,320
Congratulations,

214
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,080
now you can clash openly

215
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,560
and legitimately.

216
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,400
Seeing is believing.

217
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:23,080
They always say Wind Rider Battalion's training is worth watching,

218
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,880
that it's thoughtful and innovative.

219
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,960
So this is their innovation, huh?

220
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,560
Today, Guo Zijian, right in front of Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

221
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:32,720
directly challenged me.

222
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:35,440
I really don't know where he gets his confidence.

223
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,640
Exactly.

224
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:38,280
Don't worry, Battalion Commander.

225
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:39,560
In this competition,

226
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:40,920
we guarantee we'll wipe out Wind Rider Battalion.

227
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:42,960
This time, it's either us

228
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,400
or them.

229
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,880
We'll step over Wind Rider Battalion to take the red flag.

230
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:47,440
Yeah!

231
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,160
Step over them and take the red flag!

232
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:49,840
Battalion Commander,

233
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:50,800
we have to crush them.

234
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:51,920
Right, brothers?

235
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:54,040
Crush them! Crush them!

236
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:57,920
Wind Rider Battalion

237
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,280
may have dropped the ball during this drill,

238
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:01,840
but

239
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,560
their overall skills

240
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,440
are still solid.

241
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:08,400
We cannot underestimate them.

242
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:10,560
Understood?

243
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:12,920
After each company returns,

244
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,760
organize maneuvers immediately.

245
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:16,280
This time,

246
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:18,960
we will redeem ourselves

247
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,240
and crush Wind Rider Battalion.

248
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:23,120
Is that clear?

249
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,000
Clear!

250
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,640
Crush Wind Rider Battalion!

251
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,400
Just now,

252
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,760
we dropped by Hurricane Battalion to do some recon.

253
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,680
Their enthusiasm for training is way higher than ours.

254
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:43,520
Report!

255
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:44,560
Come in.

256
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:45,200
Battalion Commander.

257
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:46,800
Battalion Commander!

258
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:48,200
Um...

259
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,000
Hurricane...

260
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,760
What's the rush?

261
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:52,840
Take your time.

262
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,800
Hurricane Battalion wants to fight our platoon leader!

263
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,400
Tan Ke.

264
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:07,280
You're the top killer of our Hurricane Battalion.

265
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:08,640
Teach him a lesson.

266
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,640
Yeah, teach him a lesson.

267
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,000
I heard

268
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,120
you're known as the King of Soldiers.

269
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,640
That's just my comrades

270
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:20,680
joking around.

271
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,080
It's just hype.

272
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:25,440
Just hype.

273
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,320
Since you've got no skills,

274
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:29,560
keep your tail between your legs.

275
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,800
Don't be so arrogant.

276
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,080
Squad Leader Tan,

277
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:34,720
am I arrogant?

278
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:36,000
You think you aren't?

279
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:39,120
You ruined Old Wu's Golden Right Foot.

280
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,880
And you purposely transferred to our 396th Brigade.

281
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,880
You think there's no one in the 396th to stop you?

282
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,680
What else do you want?

283
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,280
Do you really think

284
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:51,160
that in our 396th Brigade,

285
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,920
among all the scouts,

286
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,440
there's truly no one who can deal with you?

287
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,400
I've never thought that.

288
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,120
Actually, you know it yourself.

289
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,400
Other than the New-Type Company,

290
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,440
hardly anyone in the Wind Rider Battalion likes you.

291
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:09,000
Do you know why Lin Yihu

292
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,560
begged everyone

293
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,160
to be transferred under your command?

294
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:14,640
Old Tan.

295
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:15,680
What are you talking about?

296
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:17,880
Don't listen to his nonsense.

297
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,240
Lin Yihu,

298
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,040
there's nothing to hide.

299
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,720
Tell him clearly today

300
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:27,240
that you transferred under him

301
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,760
just to avenge Old Wu.

302
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:31,280
Just to find a chance to teach him a good lesson.

303
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:32,880
Watch your mouth!

304
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:34,640
That's out of line.

305
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,560
Relax, brother.

306
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,960
I'll be honorable right now.

307
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,840
How about it, Yang Maolin?

308
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,400
There's no time like the present.

309
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,440
Let's spar.

310
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:46,520
Squad Leader Tan,

311
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,800
I know you've got skills,

312
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:50,760
but I don't want to fight.

313
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:51,600
Don't want to?

314
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:53,800
Or don't dare to?

315
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,160
I don't dare.

316
00:13:58,720 --> 00:13:59,720
Think what you want.

317
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:01,720
Fine.

318
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,120
Brothers of the Hurricane Battalion,

319
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,040
you all heard him.

320
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:10,440
Wind Rider Special Ops Acting Platoon Leader Yang Maolin,

321
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:13,120
surrendered without a fight!

322
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:15,560
Surrendered without a fight!

323
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:19,920
Surrendered! Surrendered!

324
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:22,760
There's no need to rub it in.

325
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,400
Since he already admitted defeat,

326
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:25,280
let it go.

327
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,720
Let's just treat him like dirt

328
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,120
and let him go.

329
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:32,000
Treat him like dirt and let him go!

330
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,040
Treat him like dirt and let him go!

331
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,920
Alright, let him go.

332
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:39,600
Move out!

333
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,200
Tan Ke.

334
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:42,520
Come back!

335
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,040
You got that right.

336
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,680
Our recon squad does have a grudge against Yang Maolin.

337
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:00,200
But that's family business between us brothers.

338
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,080
Don't forget.

339
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:02,800
We're opponents now.

340
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,160
Things have changed.

341
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,280
Hey, Lin Yihu.

342
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:08,000
What are you getting so worked up about?

343
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:10,680
If Yang Maolin were still in the 404th Brigade,

344
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:12,440
I'd fight him alongside you.

345
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:16,440
But Yang Maolin is in the Wind Rider Battalion now.

346
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,320
And he's my direct superior.

347
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,960
Insulting my platoon leader right to our faces

348
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:21,920
is just unacceptable.

349
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,160
Unacceptable.

350
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:27,920
Lin Yihu,

351
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:29,720
if you want to stand up for him,

352
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:31,440
you two can fight it out.

353
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:32,760
I'm not getting involved.

354
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:33,880
Then what are you doing?

355
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,120
I'm stepping up today

356
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,440
just to tell Yang Maolin

357
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,560
that he represents the Wind Rider Battalion.

358
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:40,800
Standing behind him

359
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:43,040
are hundreds of his Wind Rider Battalion brothers.

360
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,600
Right.

361
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,800
Wind Rider Battalion Recon Squad,

362
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:50,520
Lin Yihu.

363
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,880
And me, Recon Squad's Ding Shaolong.

364
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,640
Recon Squad's Xu Chunxiao.

365
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:55,360
Wind Rider Battalion!

366
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:58,200
And me! And me!

367
00:15:58,600 --> 00:15:59,920
Electronic Countermeasures Squad Leader, Hong Xiafei.

368
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,000
Platoon Leader Yang!

369
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,480
Show them what the King of Soldiers can do!

370
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,600
Let them see it!

371
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,680
Yeah, let them see it!

372
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,240
Yeah!

373
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,160
Show them what the King of Soldiers can do!

374
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:09,920
Lin Yihu,

375
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,600
you were my classmate.

376
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:13,360
All that dirt on Yang Maolin,

377
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,800
didn't you tell me all of it?

378
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:15,160
Yes.

379
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:16,400
I told you.

380
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,120
Being old classmates is one thing,

381
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,640
being comrades is another. Two different things.

382
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,120
For the rest of my life,

383
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,760
I might never be friends with Yang Maolin.

384
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,960
But on the battlefield,

385
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:27,760
I'd take a bullet for him.

386
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,320
I'd give my life for him.

387
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,240
Fine.

388
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:38,640
Fair enough.

389
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:43,280
In that case, Yang Maolin,

390
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,840
there's nothing more for us to say.

391
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,760
Show us what you've got.

392
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:50,440
Yang Maolin,

393
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,000
remember this.

394
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:53,840
You are not alone.

395
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:58,160
You have us.

396
00:16:58,880 --> 00:16:59,320
And me.

397
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,040
And me.

398
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:00,280
And me.

399
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:00,760
And me.

400
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:01,400
And me.

401
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,160
Honey Badger!

402
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,320
Fight!

403
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:17,320
Hurricane Battalion cheerleaders!

404
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,480
Here!

405
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,440
What's going on?

406
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:20,960
Victory!

407
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,000
Two soldiers from Wind Rider Battalion and Hurricane Battalion

408
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,000
are sparring.

409
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,080
Platoon Leader Yang,

410
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:27,040
Victory!

411
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,280
Squad Leader Tan,

412
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,200
Victory!

413
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,280
What if they get hurt?

414
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:33,880
Why aren't you keeping an eye on them?

415
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,920
Battalion Commanders Guo and Jiang are both there.

416
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:36,560
They'll be fine.

417
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:38,800
Commander Guo,

418
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,760
the key soldiers of our two battalions

419
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,360
want to spar.

420
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:45,040
What do you think?

421
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,600
Sparring and exchanging skills

422
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:47,720
is a good thing.

423
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,000
Good.

424
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,840
Tan Ke! Yang Maolin!

425
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:52,520
Here!

426
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:53,000
Here!

427
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:54,840
Right now,

428
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:57,400
the military commanders of both battalions

429
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:58,440
are here.

430
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,400
Your request to spar

431
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:01,480
has been approved.

432
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:02,880
However,

433
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,200
it must not affect tomorrow's training.

434
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:05,920
Understood!

435
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:07,000
Yang Maolin,

436
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,920
things outside the ring

437
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:12,480
have been settled.

438
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:13,960
Things inside the ring

439
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,200
are now up to you.

440
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:17,160
Understood!

441
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,000
Who is sparring?

442
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:21,960
Yang Maolin from Wind Rider Battalion and Tan Ke from Hurricane Battalion.

443
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,080
Yang Maolin.

444
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:24,840
That guy...

445
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:27,440
he's exactly like that... what do you call it?

446
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:30,080
Everyone gave him the nickname Honey Badger.

447
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:30,640
Exactly.

448
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:31,640
Honey Badger.

449
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:34,680
It's an African animal, a honey badger.

450
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:35,760
I know, I know.

451
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,240
The one that fights anyone it meets.

452
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,800
It's small but dares to challenge lions.

453
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:40,000
I know, I know. That's enough.

454
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,440
Get back to work. Yes, sir.

455
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:43,800
Commander Guo,

456
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:45,840
that's not fair, is it?

457
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:50,560
That's playing dirty.

458
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,960
Honey Badger!

459
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:53,000
Go!

460
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:54,480
Platoon Leader Yang!

461
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,800
Go!

462
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,960
Honey Badger!

463
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:57,960
Go!

464
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:00,200
Sorry. All is fair in war.

465
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,520
You fell for such a cheap trick.

466
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,560
Guess you're not much of a King of Soldiers.

467
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,480
My mistake.

468
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,920
I treated you like a comrade just now.

469
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,520
Since when are there comrades on the battlefield?

470
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,400
Only opponents.

471
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:29,440
Come on!

472
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:30,800
Beautiful!

473
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:33,480
Come on!

474
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:35,160
Come on!

475
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:36,920
Come on!

476
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:38,640
Come on!

477
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:06,640
Alright.

478
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,720
Yang Maolin.

479
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,560
What's so funny?

480
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,760
Is it really that funny?

481
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:33,240
We're all comrades.

482
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:34,400
You didn't have to hit so hard.

483
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,000
This is your punishment.

484
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:37,160
Learned your lesson?

485
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:40,760
Battalion Commander Guo,

486
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:42,840
I can tell.

487
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,040
This Platoon Leader Yang of yours

488
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:48,720
really can't act.

489
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:50,360
And you

490
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,440
aren't that good at it either.

491
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:55,720
Tan Ke!

492
00:20:58,080 --> 00:20:58,520
Here!

493
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:00,560
Are you okay?

494
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:01,560
Commander.

495
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:02,080
I'm sorry.

496
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:02,920
I lost.

497
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,760
It's not about winning or losing.

498
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:06,440
It was just a sparring match.

499
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:07,960
Right?

500
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,320
There's always next time.

501
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:11,360
Hurricane Battalion!

502
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:12,480
Form up and move out!

503
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:14,880
Hurricane Battalion,

504
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:15,600
attention!

505
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:23,960
You're so dumb.

506
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:25,880
All you know is how to fight.

507
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:27,120
You can't even put on an act.

508
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:29,360
If you're ever sent on an undercover mission,

509
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:29,960
what are you gonna do?

510
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:31,160
Battalion Commander Guo,

511
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:33,320
Platoon Leader Yang helped us win the match.

512
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:34,760
He's a hero, no matter what.

513
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:36,080
We shouldn't treat a hero like this.

514
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:37,640
Exactly.

515
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:40,720
Right?

516
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,000
Yeah!

517
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:43,920
Squad Leader Hong is right.

518
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:46,000
Today, Yang Maolin

519
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:48,120
is the hero of our Wind Rider Battalion.

520
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,600
How should we treat a hero?

521
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,480
Toss him in the air!

522
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:54,920
Then what are you waiting for?

523
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:00,440
One, two, three!

524
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,800
One, two, three!

525
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:04,560
This Yang Maolin

526
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:06,640
didn't let Wu Dongsheng down after all.

527
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,280
Squad Leader Wu,

528
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:11,120
do you know

529
00:22:11,120 --> 00:22:11,800
why Yang Maolin

530
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:13,880
came to the 396th Brigade?

531
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,160
Wu Dongsheng told him to.

532
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,440
He promised Wu Dongsheng

533
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:25,720
that he would continue on the path

534
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,400
Wu couldn't finish.

535
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:31,000
He even wrote a pledge in blood.

536
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:32,600
Yihu,

537
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,320
when Old Wu had his accident,

538
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,680
he took it harder than anyone.

539
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:42,440
But he has always

540
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:44,920
remembered

541
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:47,240
his promise to Wu Dongsheng.

542
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:48,680
Commander,

543
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,200
why didn't you say this sooner?

544
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:52,960
I didn't say anything

545
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:55,880
because I wanted Yang Maolin

546
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:58,240
to use his own abilities

547
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:00,520
to earn everyone's trust.

548
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:32,040
Lin Yihu

549
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:33,840
Thanks.

550
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:35,200
Alright.

551
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:36,760
Don't overthink it.

552
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,000
I didn't help you earlier for selfish reasons.

553
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,800
That's why I respect you.

554
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,600
This is also what

555
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:45,960
Squad Leader Wu gave me before...

556
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,160
Don't mention him in front of me.

557
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:50,360
Fine.

558
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:51,280
I won't.

559
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:58,800
It's all fate.

560
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:00,960
Alright.

561
00:24:03,040 --> 00:24:04,360
What happened between us is in the past.

562
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:06,240
But Squad Leader Wu's accident...

563
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:08,200
Even though he says he doesn't blame you,

564
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:10,440
I haven't completely gotten over it myself.

565
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:13,440
I understand all that.

566
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,600
But as for me,

567
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:18,400
I just stubbornly cling to my own principles.

568
00:24:18,760 --> 00:24:19,480
I understand.

569
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:26,880
Platoon Leader Yang.

570
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:26,040
Two

571
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:28,680
Three

572
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:32,560
Four

573
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:15,560
How are you driving?

574
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Dong Zhenguo!

575
00:26:21,320 --> 00:26:22,440
What's the meaning of this?

576
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:24,960
Your IFV was either charging blindly...

577
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:26,160
...or swerving all over the place.

578
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:27,400
How are we supposed to coordinate with you?

579
00:26:27,600 --> 00:26:29,240
Do you even know what tactical coordination is?

580
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:30,960
Don't play the big shot with me.

581
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:32,080
This kind of coordination...

582
00:26:32,080 --> 00:26:34,040
...is a classic case of tanks leading an infantry charge.

583
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:35,880
It's such a classic theory.

584
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:37,640
I just adapted it a bit.

585
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:38,480
What's wrong with that?

586
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,000
Let me tell you,

587
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:43,000
assault guns have their own rules.

588
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:45,360
You were full of sweet talk when you came here,

589
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:46,880
and afraid I'd steal your thunder.

590
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:48,480
Who knew that after all this time,

591
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:49,480
you're just using outdated tactics.

592
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:50,640
Good thing that today,

593
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:51,760
I got three veteran commanders driving.

594
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:52,720
Otherwise,

595
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:53,760
there definitely would've been an accident.

596
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:54,440
Alright, alright.

597
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:55,360
Don't make it sound so scary.

598
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:57,200
Let's just drop this.

599
00:26:57,800 --> 00:26:58,720
I'll buy you a meal sometime.

600
00:26:58,800 --> 00:26:59,760
Buy me a meal?

601
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:01,040
We almost crashed into each other.

602
00:27:01,040 --> 00:27:01,840
And you're talking about food?

603
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:03,280
Well, we didn't crash, did we?

604
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:04,000
If we had...

605
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:11,960
What is going on here?

606
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:13,160
Chief!

607
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:20,480
My goodness.

608
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:23,560
What are you two doing?

609
00:27:26,040 --> 00:27:26,960
Are you playing around?

610
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:28,600
With two company commanders present,

611
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,760
you almost caused a major accident.

612
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,320
In all my years in the military,

613
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,320
it is the first time I have seen training like this.

614
00:27:36,640 --> 00:27:37,360
What were you doing?

615
00:27:38,520 --> 00:27:39,280
Running away?

616
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,960
We were practicing new tactics.

617
00:27:42,320 --> 00:27:43,280
We just started combined training,

618
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:44,920
so it is a bit unstable.

619
00:27:44,920 --> 00:27:45,840
Do not give me that nonsense.

620
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,600
This is all newly issued equipment.

621
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:50,320
If it gets damaged,

622
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:51,560
who is going to take responsibility?

623
00:27:57,120 --> 00:27:57,640
Deputy Brigade Commander,

624
00:27:58,360 --> 00:27:59,000
Guo Zijian!

625
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:00,480
Come here.

626
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:01,440
Take a look at this.

627
00:28:02,360 --> 00:28:03,120
Take a good look.

628
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:06,640
I will not waste words.

629
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:08,000
Starting from now,

630
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:09,000
training is suspended for one day.

631
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:09,960
No,

632
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:11,200
three days.

633
00:28:11,840 --> 00:28:14,080
Battalions, companies, platoons, and squads,

634
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:15,920
conduct a level-by-level inspection.

635
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:18,880
Search for potential hazards,

636
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:20,200
formulate countermeasures,

637
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:22,400
and thoroughly rectify them.

638
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:23,720
Yes, sir!

639
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:24,400
Yes, sir!

640
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:26,440
Every single one of you,

641
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:28,640
write down your reflections.

642
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:30,200
Including you.

643
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:31,280
Yes, sir!

644
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:48,200
Battalion Commander.

645
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,400
Sorry.

646
00:28:49,560 --> 00:28:50,720
I was too eager for results.

647
00:28:50,960 --> 00:28:52,040
I was a bit too impatient.

648
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:54,160
You really know how to cause me trouble.

649
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:56,160
So what do we do now?

650
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:57,040
What do you mean, what do we do?

651
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:00,000
Go back and rewrite the training plan.

652
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:01,840
Submit it to me as soon as it's done.

653
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:03,000
Yes, sir.

654
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,120
Drive the vehicle back.

655
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:09,960
Look what you've done.

656
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:14,760
Report.

657
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:15,480
Come in.

658
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:19,160
What is it?

659
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:20,400
Battalion Commander.

660
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:23,760
All combined drills are suspended.

661
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:24,520
Pending rectification.

662
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:25,280
Why?

663
00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:27,600
Two companies from the Wind Rider Battalion were drilling new tactics.

664
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:28,600
They were running wild.

665
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:31,160
They almost crashed the newly equipped

666
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:31,920
assault guns head-on.

667
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:34,000
And Deputy Brigade Commander Suo happened to see it.

668
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:38,800
Guo Zijian, Guo Zijian.

669
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,240
This careless habit of yours

670
00:29:43,680 --> 00:29:44,720
really needs to change.

671
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:55,360
Deputy Brigade Commander.

672
00:29:57,280 --> 00:29:59,080
I was wondering why I couldn't find you at headquarters.

673
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:00,320
What brings you here?

674
00:30:01,520 --> 00:30:02,320
Do you need something?

675
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:03,760
It's like this.

676
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:06,560
Dong Zhenguo and Gao Peng stayed up all night last night

677
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:09,040
and finished the first phase of the training plan.

678
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:09,960
Please review and approve it.

679
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:17,160
Do you know Murphy's Law?

680
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:18,160
I do.

681
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,240
Do you think

682
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,200
that all I have on my mind

683
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:26,720
is just the word "safety"?

684
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:30,640
I'll be honest with you.

685
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:33,360
I started out as a military officer.

686
00:30:34,320 --> 00:30:35,320
I don't approve of

687
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:38,000
overemphasizing safety.

688
00:30:38,480 --> 00:30:39,240
And I especially object to

689
00:30:39,480 --> 00:30:41,680
sacrificing combat power to guarantee safety.

690
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:43,880
But,

691
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,720
that doesn't mean

692
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:47,640
I'll abandon my principles.

693
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:49,400
Safety isn't the center of gravity,

694
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,640
but if a safety issue arises,

695
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:53,520
it will shift that center,

696
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:55,520
and impact it.

697
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:57,440
The Deputy Brigade Commander is right.

698
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:03,880
You think that by changing this training plan,

699
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:05,840
accidents won't happen?

700
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:07,120
Let me tell you the truth.

701
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:10,240
That's absolutely impossible.

702
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,800
Murphy's Law was coined by foreigners,

703
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:15,400
but

704
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:17,600
it's not uncommon in Chinese history.

705
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:19,000
It happens all the time.

706
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:22,360
Let me share some words from the heart.

707
00:31:23,280 --> 00:31:24,080
Last night,

708
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:26,040
I didn't sleep a wink.

709
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,480
Whenever I closed my eyes,

710
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:30,640
I saw two brand new armored vehicles.

711
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,040
How can we not rectify this?

712
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,760
We appreciate your good intentions, Deputy Brigade Commander.

713
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:46,080
I know you're doing this for our own good.

714
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:47,840
But Deputy Brigade Commander,

715
00:31:48,720 --> 00:31:50,240
this training mission itself

716
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:51,400
is a

717
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:54,040
high-risk operation simulating real combat.

718
00:31:56,200 --> 00:31:58,240
So everything I just said was for nothing?

719
00:31:58,560 --> 00:31:59,040
No.

720
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,600
What I mean is,

721
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:02,040
looking globally,

722
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,040
in any country,

723
00:32:03,320 --> 00:32:05,240
the military with the strongest real combat capability

724
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:06,520
is bound to be the one with

725
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,160
the highest accident rate during training.

726
00:32:08,320 --> 00:32:10,320
So I should praise you for what happened yesterday?

727
00:32:11,040 --> 00:32:12,040
I didn't mean that.

728
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:12,880
Guo Zijian,

729
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:15,400
if anyone else were arguing with me here today,

730
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:16,680
I could accept it.

731
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:18,840
I'd feel a bit better.

732
00:32:19,400 --> 00:32:20,400
But you...

733
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:22,440
For crying out loud.

734
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:24,920
Don't you have any self-awareness?

735
00:32:27,040 --> 00:32:27,600
Deputy Brigade Commander,

736
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:29,880
I don't understand what you mean.

737
00:32:30,640 --> 00:32:32,320
I train the troops to real combat standards.

738
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:33,680
Is there a problem with that?

739
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,560
You forget the pain once the wound has healed.

740
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:38,120
Do you really need

741
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:39,680
incidents like Wu Dongsheng's to happen again

742
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:41,000
before you mature?

743
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,280
Liu!

744
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:44,760
Here!

745
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:46,800
Let's go.

746
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:47,400
Yes, sir.

747
00:32:59,440 --> 00:32:59,840
Battalion Commander.

748
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:01,080
What should we do?

749
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:03,240
What else can we do?

750
00:33:05,120 --> 00:33:05,720
Rectify.

751
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:11,800
Publicity work

752
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:12,720
is an important part of our Party

753
00:33:12,720 --> 00:33:14,840
and our military's political work.

754
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:16,120
Right now,

755
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:18,040
the media is very interested

756
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:19,320
in our new-type combined forces.

757
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:21,920
These reporters used to be so arrogant.

758
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:24,880
Now they're coming to us to sing our praises.

759
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:26,200
So,

760
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,400
we must make sure

761
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:28,280
to give them a good report

762
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:29,240
and host them well.

763
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:30,840
Yes,

764
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:33,200
Chief.

765
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:35,920
Getting famous and drawing attention

766
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,240
isn't necessarily a good thing.

767
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:41,120
Everything has two sides.

768
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:43,280
We need to analyze specific situations.

769
00:33:43,520 --> 00:33:43,960
Right?

770
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:46,560
Just because you dislike drawing attention,

771
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,680
you shouldn't be prejudiced against publicity.

772
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:51,080
You're right, Chief.

773
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:53,520
But I feel nothing is set in stone yet,

774
00:33:53,760 --> 00:33:54,960
and we're already building public hype.

775
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:58,040
If the Value Cube doesn't hold much value,

776
00:33:58,040 --> 00:33:59,120
or even loses its value entirely,

777
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:01,040
how will we justify it then?

778
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:02,960
The rule of journalism

779
00:34:02,960 --> 00:34:05,080
is to report on new things.

780
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:06,600
As for where these new things

781
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:08,280
will head,

782
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,320
or what they will turn out to be,

783
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,320
no one can control that.

784
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:12,800
How can you link the two together?

785
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:14,440
You need to improve your awareness.

786
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:16,640
I just can't get past this.

787
00:34:16,640 --> 00:34:18,000
The fact that you can't get past it

788
00:34:18,560 --> 00:34:20,120
shows that in your mind,

789
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:21,920
you have a lot of ego.

790
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:27,120
Of course,

791
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:28,920
regarding what to publicize,

792
00:34:29,040 --> 00:34:29,920
we can

793
00:34:30,640 --> 00:34:32,160
set requirements and lay down rules.

794
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:34,120
But we can't just use that

795
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,560
as an excuse to flatly refuse

796
00:34:36,680 --> 00:34:37,960
or even respond negatively.

797
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,400
Neither is a solution.

798
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:44,320
So you're saying

799
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,920
that you support this, Chief.

800
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:49,800
Don't try to trap me, kid.

801
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,120
I wouldn't dare.

802
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:53,120
This is an order from our superiors,

803
00:34:53,120 --> 00:34:54,160
so of course we must execute it.

804
00:34:55,120 --> 00:34:55,600
Alright,

805
00:34:56,760 --> 00:34:57,560
the basic principles

806
00:34:57,560 --> 00:34:58,560
have already been made clear.

807
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:01,160
Handle the specifics as you see fit.

808
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:07,040
I guarantee to complete the mission.

809
00:35:12,720 --> 00:35:13,480
Reporting, Chief.

810
00:35:14,440 --> 00:35:15,480
I reserve my personal opinion.

811
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:18,240
I don't think this is the best time.

812
00:35:20,920 --> 00:35:21,720
Ling Jun.

813
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:24,160
Guo Zijian is already enough of a headache.

814
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:26,440
Why is it that after you came to the 396th Brigade,

815
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:28,240
you've become just like him?

816
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:29,040
Report,

817
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:30,400
You are the company you keep,

818
00:35:30,760 --> 00:35:32,520
and the bad influence works fast.

819
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:33,680
Let's consider the rectification

820
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:35,200
settled for now.

821
00:35:36,440 --> 00:35:38,400
I'm going to the Special Ops Platoon to arrange their training.

822
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:39,680
You're a Battalion Commander,

823
00:35:39,680 --> 00:35:41,200
why are you keeping such a close eye on a platoon's training?

824
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:42,800
Hurry up and get ready to go to the interview with me.

825
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:44,200
Your presence at the interview is enough.

826
00:35:45,120 --> 00:35:45,880
From the start of field training until now,

827
00:35:45,880 --> 00:35:47,160
we haven't been allowed a single live-equipment joint drill.

828
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:48,200
What am I supposed to say?

829
00:35:48,600 --> 00:35:49,600
I have nothing to say.

830
00:35:49,880 --> 00:35:51,640
I can't be the only one at the interview.

831
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:52,880
Look at his attitude.

832
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:53,600
Guo Zijian!

833
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:56,040
Staff Officer Liang, then you come with me.

834
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:57,160
Instructor, I'll leave it to you then.

835
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:00,280
Staff Officer Hu.

836
00:36:01,640 --> 00:36:02,280
Where are you going?

837
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:04,440
I'm going to the restroom.

838
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:08,960
Then hurry back.

839
00:36:15,240 --> 00:36:17,320
Before Brigade Commander Xu left for the group army meeting,

840
00:36:17,320 --> 00:36:18,080
he specifically instructed

841
00:36:18,520 --> 00:36:19,720
that this interview

842
00:36:20,280 --> 00:36:21,920
is focused solely on the Wind Rider Battalion.

843
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:24,240
The theme revolves around the vanguard battalion's development.

844
00:36:24,840 --> 00:36:25,600
He also mentioned

845
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:27,600
that Deputy Corps Commander Liang will come in person,

846
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:29,400
and told us to make sure the reception goes perfectly.

847
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:31,120
Where is Guo Zijian?

848
00:36:32,160 --> 00:36:33,920
He's organizing training for the special ops platoon.

849
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:35,680
That guy...

850
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:39,280
doesn't know how to prioritize his work.

851
00:36:42,040 --> 00:36:42,400
Wang Yuan.

852
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:45,600
Be a bit more welcoming when the reporters get here.

853
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:46,480
Yes.

854
00:36:46,640 --> 00:36:47,720
Stop pulling a long face.

855
00:36:48,600 --> 00:36:49,080
Isn't that right, Hai Tian?

856
00:36:49,160 --> 00:36:50,640
Of course. Always ready.

857
00:37:07,040 --> 00:37:07,880
Welcome, welcome.

858
00:37:08,520 --> 00:37:09,280
Thank you all for your hard work.

859
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,520
Reporter Luo, I've heard so much about you.

860
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:16,240
I am Suo Jian'an, Deputy Brigade Commander of the 396th Brigade.

861
00:37:16,440 --> 00:37:17,880
I will be in charge of hosting you today.

862
00:37:18,160 --> 00:37:19,760
Currently, the interview schedule

863
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:20,680
has already been arranged.

864
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:23,360
The Chief is here.

865
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:28,840
Chief, the reporters have arrived.

866
00:37:28,840 --> 00:37:29,360
Reporter Luo.

867
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:31,480
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

868
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:31,960
Deputy Corps Commander Liang.

869
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:32,800
I'm not late, am I?

870
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:33,760
We meet again.

871
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:35,560
I saw your name on the list,

872
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:36,440
so I made a special trip here.

873
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:37,960
Having you here gives me peace of mind.

874
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:39,840
This time, our promotional campaign's

875
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:40,520
depth,

876
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:40,800
breadth,

877
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:41,400
and impact

878
00:37:41,640 --> 00:37:42,280
will be completely different.

879
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:43,880
You flatter me.

880
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:44,680
Let's go.

881
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:45,200
Alright.

882
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:45,720
I'll accompany you in.

883
00:37:45,720 --> 00:37:46,280
Okay. After you.

884
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:56,160
Squad Leader.

885
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,200
What's the point of us doing this?

886
00:37:58,640 --> 00:37:59,960
Polishing this place like a mirror...

887
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:00,760
Is this useful in a war?

888
00:38:00,960 --> 00:38:02,040
That's enough, Dongfang.

889
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:04,520
Barracks maintenance is a comprehensive test for a soldier.

890
00:38:04,600 --> 00:38:05,680
Only by sticking to it long-term

891
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:07,720
can you maintain that resilience on the battlefield.

892
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:08,800
You brat.

893
00:38:08,800 --> 00:38:09,840
How many times have I explained this to you?

894
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:10,560
You just don't get it.

895
00:38:12,200 --> 00:38:14,000
I'll never get the hang of this in my life.

896
00:38:14,720 --> 00:38:15,280
Alright.

897
00:38:15,800 --> 00:38:16,520
Both of you, drop it.

898
00:38:17,120 --> 00:38:17,920
If you have this much free time,

899
00:38:18,760 --> 00:38:20,760
go clear the drainage ditches beside the tent.

900
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:24,040
Platoon Leader, aren't you frustrated?

901
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:26,000
I mean, look at this great weather,

902
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:26,800
this great environment,

903
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:28,160
and this great training ground.

904
00:38:28,200 --> 00:38:29,000
And what about us?

905
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:30,800
We're just here doing prep work

906
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:31,560
or hosting guests.

907
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:32,240
What's the point?

908
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:35,720
It's not hosting, it's a press interview.

909
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,560
This is a great chance for our Wind Rider Battalion to step into the spotlight.

910
00:38:38,800 --> 00:38:39,880
Spotlight? What spotlight?

911
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:41,040
What's there to show off?

912
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:42,320
What are the reporters here to cover?

913
00:38:42,560 --> 00:38:43,360
Cover this dirt?

914
00:38:43,560 --> 00:38:44,520
There's nothing to film.

915
00:38:54,720 --> 00:38:56,320
Less complaining from now on.

916
00:38:57,160 --> 00:38:57,760
Talking too much about it

917
00:38:58,720 --> 00:38:59,960
doesn't just affect you,

918
00:39:00,480 --> 00:39:02,360
it brings down your comrades, too.

919
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:03,360
Battalion Commander.

920
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:05,280
No one is allowed to bring this up again.

921
00:39:05,920 --> 00:39:07,760
A soldier's duty is to obey orders.

922
00:39:08,120 --> 00:39:09,920
Stop constantly second-guessing

923
00:39:10,040 --> 00:39:10,840
your superiors' orders.

924
00:39:11,720 --> 00:39:11,960
Yes, sir.

925
00:39:11,960 --> 00:39:12,240
Yes, sir.

926
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:12,800
Yes, sir.

927
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:16,720
Half of you will train,

928
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:17,760
and the other half will clean up.

929
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:18,880
Rotate every hour.

930
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:19,920
Great.

931
00:39:20,680 --> 00:39:21,560
Static training

932
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:22,800
in the dorms.

933
00:39:23,560 --> 00:39:24,200
That works.

934
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:25,560
Xiaoyun, Zhengzheng.

935
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:26,080
Get the equipment.

936
00:39:26,200 --> 00:39:26,640
Let's go.

937
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:32,720
Battalion Commander.

938
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,480
I'd like to talk to you alone.

939
00:39:44,360 --> 00:39:45,480
You've been acting a bit off lately.

940
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:48,640
Off how?

941
00:39:50,080 --> 00:39:51,120
In every way.

942
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:54,600
Is it because

943
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:57,240
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo

944
00:39:57,280 --> 00:39:58,720
told you about Wu Dongsheng that day?

945
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:02,960
Did Dong Zhenguo tell you that?

946
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:05,760
The comrades are all concerned about you.

947
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:09,280
Don't listen to his nonsense.

948
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:10,440
I'm fine.

949
00:40:15,240 --> 00:40:16,400
I think some things

950
00:40:17,120 --> 00:40:19,360
are better shared than kept to yourself.

951
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:21,520
What?

952
00:40:22,560 --> 00:40:25,080
Is Staff Officer Liang playing psychologist now?

953
00:40:33,840 --> 00:40:34,640
We're comrades-in-arms.

954
00:40:35,960 --> 00:40:36,920
If we were in combat,

955
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:39,680
we'd trust each other to watch our backs.

956
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:42,720
If your psychological state

957
00:40:42,720 --> 00:40:44,800
affects your judgment as a commander,

958
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:46,560
then I also

959
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:48,520
have to bear all the consequences of your actions.

960
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:50,280
So your problem

961
00:40:50,960 --> 00:40:52,400
isn't just yours alone.

962
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:54,840
It concerns the entire Wind Rider Battalion.

963
00:40:55,680 --> 00:40:57,480
Or do you think I'm not worthy of your trust?

964
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:08,320
Reporter Luo.

965
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:10,200
You haven't been to this training ground before, have you?

966
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:10,960
That's right.

967
00:41:13,040 --> 00:41:14,320
Chief, this way, please.

968
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:16,000
This is our field camp.

969
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:17,680
Battalion Commander,

970
00:41:19,080 --> 00:41:20,720
our Value Cube

971
00:41:20,720 --> 00:41:22,120
has only just started being built.

972
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:22,920
If you were to...

973
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:24,200
What Value Cube?

974
00:41:25,480 --> 00:41:26,840
It's nothing but a pile of

975
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:28,800
scrap metal that won't even turn!

976
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:39,720
Guo Zijian!

977
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:41,760
That's right.

978
00:41:43,080 --> 00:41:44,480
You were the one who proposed the Value Cube.

979
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:46,000
But together,

980
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:47,920
we've done so much research and validation.

981
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:49,040
Saying this now

982
00:41:49,040 --> 00:41:50,520
is highly irresponsible.

983
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,720
But is a Wind Rider Battalion like this

984
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:54,720
really what we want to see

985
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:56,520
as our new-type combat forces?

986
00:41:57,560 --> 00:41:59,040
We finally deployed the troops out here,

987
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:01,400
yet we can't run a single live-equipment drill.

988
00:42:01,760 --> 00:42:03,360
Every day is about safety and rectification.

989
00:42:04,160 --> 00:42:05,640
We've submitted piles of reports and plans,

990
00:42:05,760 --> 00:42:07,080
but made absolutely zero progress.

991
00:42:07,080 --> 00:42:09,080
But there's nothing wrong with focusing on safety.

992
00:42:09,080 --> 00:42:10,440
Of course I know there isn't.

993
00:42:13,400 --> 00:42:14,480
What happened to Wu Dongsheng,

994
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:17,520
I will never forget for the rest of my life.

995
00:42:19,320 --> 00:42:21,040
Every soldier is someone's child.

996
00:42:21,960 --> 00:42:24,120
I watched each of them grow up step by step.

997
00:42:24,560 --> 00:42:26,240
If anything happens to any of them,

998
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:28,440
I could never forgive myself.

999
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:33,120
But if we truly want to develop new-type combat forces,

1000
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:36,400
and improve our combat capabilities,

1001
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:39,120
what else can we do but accelerate our training?

1002
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:41,040
That's right.

1003
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:44,200
We are in peacetime now.

1004
00:42:45,280 --> 00:42:46,240
But war

1005
00:42:46,240 --> 00:42:48,160
won't wait until you're ready.

1006
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:50,160
It might be tomorrow.

1007
00:42:50,360 --> 00:42:51,680
It might be today.
